# Cloudflare Pages rewrites for generated artifacts composed by
# .github/workflows/cloudflare-pages.yml.
#
# The deploy workflow removes DocC's per-symbol HTML shell copies to keep the
# artifact below Pages' file-count limit. The DocC app is a JavaScript shell
# backed by /docs/data/, so direct links can route through the single shell.
#
# Destination must be `/docs/` (canonical directory form), not
# `/docs/index.html`. Pages canonicalizes asset URLs ending in `/index.html`
# to their directory equivalent on upload, so a 200 rewrite to
# `/docs/index.html` silently fails to resolve and the request falls
# through to the project's homepage fallback.
/docs/documentation /docs/ 200
/docs/documentation/* /docs/ 200

# The Charts DocC archive is a second, self-contained shell mounted at
# /docs/charts/ (built from SwiftTUI/swift-tui-charts). Same rewrite shape.
/docs/charts/documentation /docs/charts/ 200
/docs/charts/documentation/* /docs/charts/ 200

# The dedicated Sextant product page was retired; Sextant is now one of the
# example tiles on /showcase/. Keep the previously published URL working.
/sextant /showcase/ 301
/sextant/* /showcase/ 301

# The /pipeline/ walkthrough cites swift-tui source files with repo-relative
# links (e.g. ../../swift-tui/Sources/...), which resolve to /swift-tui/... at
# the origin root. Route those to the source on GitHub so the citations work on
# the deployed site without rewriting the walkthrough's script.
/swift-tui/* https://github.com/SwiftTUI/swift-tui/blob/main/:splat 302
